e/crop/8139x5426+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F2e%2F44%2Fa0c105a9457e8ad979d165cae461%2Fap26137105498276.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8139x5426+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F2e%2F44%2Fa0c105a9457e8ad979d165cae461%2Fap26137105498276.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8139x5426+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F2e%2F44%2Fa0c105a9457e8ad979d165cae461%2Fap26137105498276.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8139x5426+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F2e%2F44%2Fa0c105a9457e8ad979d165cae461%2Fap26137105498276.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8139x5426+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F2e%2F44%2Fa0c105a9457e8ad979d165cae461%2Fap26137105498276.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8139x5426+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F2e%2F44%2Fa0c105a9457e8ad979d165cae461%2Fap26137105498276.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8139x5426+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F2e%2F44%2Fa0c105a9457e8ad979d165cae461%2Fap26137105498276.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8139x5426+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F2e%2F44%2Fa0c105a9457e8ad979d165cae461%2Fap26137105498276.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8139x5426+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F2e%2F44%2Fa0c105a9457e8ad979d165cae461%2Fap26137105498276.jpg" class="img" alt="Julia Letlow speaks to media during an election night watch party on May 16, 2026, in Baton Rouge, La." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Julia Letlow speaks to media during an election night watch party on May 16, 2026, in Baton Rouge, La.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Matthew Hinton/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Letlow has now made history twice. She was the first Republican woman elected to the U.S. House from Louisiana in 2021. Letlow ran for the House in a special election to replace her late husband, Congressman Luke Letlow, who died of COVID-19 in 2020. Now, Louisiana voters have decided to send her to the Senate, where she will be the first Republican woman from the state to serve. She will succeed Republican Sen. Bill Cassidy, who Letlow beat in the primary election.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Abdul El-Sayed of Michigan &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-152348" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-